[# Section 10 — migration: v0.7.x → v0.8.0, cross-format intake,
   retired surfaces. #]

[section id=migration n=10 title='Migration'

  [child id=from-v07x n=10.1 title='From v0.7.x to v0.8.0'
    [intro
      """v0.8.0 is the first stable tag after v0.7.5 (v0.7.6 was skipped
         intentionally — see backlog decision `d-2026-05-22-04`). v0.8.0
         is the pre-release API/format-stability boundary; there are no
         external users yet, so the renames below were applied directly
         across the codebase rather than shipped as user-facing tooling.
         This section is the reference for the shape of the changes."""]

    [body
      """**Rename: programs → code.** Every internal `programs`
         reference becomes `code`. The brand
         layer ("CX is data and code") was renamed immediately on
         d-2026-05-22-01; the internal rename cascades through:"""]

    [table columns=(was, is)
      [row was='cx_program_eval' is='cx_code_eval']
      [row was='vcx/programs/' is='vcx/code/']
      [row was='spec/programs.md' is='spec/code.md']
      [row was='conformance/programs.txt' is='conformance/code.txt']
      [row was='_cx_program_diagram (wasm)' is='_cx_code_diagram (wasm)']
      [row was='--- in_cxl (fixture marker)' is='--- in_code (fixture marker)']]

    [body
      """**`[?find]` is retired.** `[?find]` was always sugar for
         `[?for]` over a pattern. The migration is one of two
         forms:"""]

    [table columns=(was, is)
      [row was='[?find [user $u] :yield $u]' is='//user  or  [?for [user $u] [yield $u]]']
      [row was='[?find [user @active=true $u] :yield $u]' is='//user[@active=true]']
      [row was='[?find [user [email $e]] :yield $e]' is='//user/email']
      [row was='count([?find [user @active=true $u] :yield $u])' is='[$count //user[@active=true]]']]

    [body
      """**CXPath is now a value kind.** A path expression like `//user`
         parses to a `cx.PathNode` value, evaluates to a sequence, and
         round-trips canonically as the terse form. The retired v0.7.0
         CXPath subset is replaced by XPath 3.1 alignment — see
         [`spec/cxpath_alignment.md`](../../spec/cxpath_alignment.md)."""]

    [body
      """**Multi-arm `[?match]`.** `[?match]` now supports N arms
         with `[case …]` / `[when …]` /
         `[else …]` clause children, scalar literal patterns, `_`
         wildcard, and `[where …]` guards. The 2-arg form (single arm,
         raises `CXER0100` on miss) is preserved unchanged."""]

    [example lang=cx
      """[# v0.7.x — nested if chain (legacy slot form)                 #]
         [?if (name($n) = 'prose') :then [p $n]
              :else [?if (name($n) = 'code') :then [pre $n]
                          :else ()]]

         [# v0.8.0 — multi-arm match (clause-child form)                #]
         [?match $n
           [case [prose $p] [p $p]]
           [case [code $c]  [pre $c]]
           [else            ()]]"""]

    [body
      """**`[?modify]` is new.** There was no idiomatic update
         directive in v0.7.x — code had
         to rebuild via `[?for]`. v0.8.0 ships the eleven-action
         vocabulary (`[set V]` / `[delete]` / `[using F]` /
         `[rename N]` / `[set-attr N V]` / `[delete-attr N]` /
         `[append V]` / `[prepend V]` / `[insert-before V]` /
         `[insert-after V]` / `[replace V]`). See [[modify]]."""]

    [body
      """**Two-layer bindings.** See
         [`spec/bindings.md`](../../spec/bindings.md). Layer 1 is the
         canonical 16-method surface, identical across V/Python/Go/Rust.
         Layer 2 is opt-in host idiom packs (`cxlib.idioms` in Python,
         `cxlib/idioms` in Go, `cxlib::idioms` in Rust). v0.7.x had a
         single flat surface per binding; v0.8.0 codifies the
         separation. See [[bindings]]."""]

    [body
      """**Binding scope reduced to four.** v0.8.0 ships only V
         (native), Python, Go, Rust. The
         TypeScript, Java, C#, Ruby, Kotlin, and Swift bindings are
         moved to `lang/_archived/` (preserved, not deleted).
         Restoration is opt-in once Layer-1 is stable; community
         contributions accepted but not blocked on. The make tests for
         archived bindings are no longer in the default `make test`
         target."""]

    [note
      """The renames above are **mechanical** — they do not attempt to
         convert hand-rolled nested `[?if]` chains to multi-arm
         `[?match]` (that requires semantic understanding of what each
         branch tests). The conversion is straightforward by hand once
         you know the multi-arm form (see [[match]])."""]]

  [child id=from-xml n=10.2 title='From XML'
    [intro
      """XML is the closest projection to CX — same element / attribute /
         body shape. Migration is one-shot: `cx convert input.xml --to
         cx --out input.cx`."""]

    [list
      [item """**DOCTYPE / DTD** — drop. Use a CX schema (`.cxs`)
              instead. See [[schema]]."""]
      [item """**Namespaces** — `xmlns:*` declarations become CX
              attributes on the root element; namespace-qualified
              element names use the same `prefix:name` form. See
              [`spec/namespaces.md`](../../spec/namespaces.md)."""]
      [item """**CDATA** — projects to triple-quoted strings."""]
      [item """**Processing instructions** — preserved as `[?pi …]`
              elements; their bodies are opaque text."""]
      [item """**XPath queries** — port to CXPath. The selection core
              is identical (see
              [`spec/cxpath_alignment.md`](../../spec/cxpath_alignment.md));
              you drop XPath's `for`/`let`/`if`/`function` constructs
              in favor of the CX directives."""]
      [item """**XSLT / XQuery transforms** — port to CX code. There
              is no automated converter; the structural mapping is
              direct because the data model is the same."""]]]

  [child id=from-json-yaml n=10.3 title='From JSON / YAML / TOML'
    [intro
      """These are projection formats. Migration is again one-shot:
         `cx convert input.json --to cx --out input.cx`."""]

    [body
      """The projection rules are deterministic and reversible (see
         [[json]], [[yaml]], [[toml]]). What you gain on the CX side:"""]

    [list
      [item """**Comments.** JSON has none; YAML and TOML have ad-hoc
              comments. CX has structured `[# … #]` comments that
              survive `cx fmt` and round-trip across projections."""]
      [item """**Schemas.** JSON Schema / YAML schemas are external
              artifacts. CX schemas are first-class CX, in the same
              parser, with the same toolchain."""]
      [item """**Queries.** JSONPath / `jq` / YAML query systems are
              format-specific. CXPath works on any projected document
              regardless of source format."""]
      [item """**Updates.** No idiomatic pure-functional update for
              JSON / YAML / TOML at the format level. `[?modify]`
              gives you one."""]
      [item """**Identity.** Canonical JSON, JCS, and `jq -S` exist
              but are not universally adopted. CX has one canonical
              form built into every tool."""]]]

  [child id=retired-surfaces n=10.4 title='Retired surfaces and replacements'
    [intro
      """Surfaces removed or renamed across v0.7.x → v0.8.0, with their
         replacement."""]

    [table columns=(retired, replacement, source)
      [row retired='[?find]' replacement='[?for] over pattern, or CXPath //name'
        source='CXPath value-kind alignment']
      [row retired='[- comment -]' replacement='[# comment #]'
        source='lexer consolidation']
      [row retired=':contains predicate hack' replacement='ancestor:: axis'
        source='CXPath value-kind alignment']
      [row retired=':direct modifier hack' replacement='following-sibling:: axis'
        source='CXPath value-kind alignment']
      [row retired='XPath general-comparison =' replacement='value-comparison only'
        source='CXPath value-kind alignment']
      [row retired='cx_program_eval (C ABI)' replacement='cx_code_eval'
        source='programs → code rename']
      [row retired='in_cxl (fixture marker)' replacement='in_code'
        source='programs → code rename']
      [row retired='cxl-* playground starter ids' replacement='code-* starter ids'
        source='Phase 7.3']
      [row retired='TypeScript / Java / C# / Ruby / Kotlin / Swift bindings'
        replacement='archived under lang/_archived/'
        source='d-2026-05-22-03']
      [row retired='Layer-1-only flat binding surface' replacement='Layer 1 + Layer 2'
        source='d-2026-05-22-07']]

    [note
      """**Archived bindings are not deleted.** Files move to
         `lang/_archived/<lang>/` and remain in git history. The
         restoration path: each archived binding can return on opt-in
         once Layer 1 is stable. Community contributions are welcome
         on the archived path; they are not blocked on by the core
         team."""]

    [body
      """**Doc-gen pipeline consolidated.** v0.8.0 ships a single
         pre-publish documentation generator at
         `scripts/gen_guide/` rendering `docs-src/canonical/` into
         the multi-page guide at `docs/guide/` — eat-our-own-dog-food
         via `cx eval` on every section. See [[docgen]] for the
         pipeline and [`make guide`] for the
         entry point."""]]

  [child id=extend-contribute n=10.5 title='Extend and contribute'
    [intro
      """CX is open to contribution at every layer. This subsection is
         the developer-facing how-to: filing issues, adding fixtures,
         proposing changes, shipping a binding, debugging a failure."""]

    [child id=file-bug n=10.5.1 title='Filing an issue'
      [body
        """Issues live in the project tracker. Every report should
           include: minimal CX reproducer (one file), `cx --version`
           output, error code (e.g. CXER0103) + message, expected vs
           observed behaviour, and the workaround you used if any.
           For parse / canon / hash bugs, a 5-line CX snippet is
           usually enough; for evaluator bugs include the directive
           shape and the input doc."""]]

    [child id=add-fixture n=10.5.2 title='Adding a conformance fixture'
      [body
        """The conformance suite is `conformance/*.txt` files in
           per-feature buckets (code.txt for directives, data_bin.txt
           for binary wire, etc.). Each fixture has a `=== test: id`
           header + `--- in_cx` / `--- call` / `--- out_text` (or
           `out_err`) blocks. To add one:"""]
      [list
        [item """Identify the right file (`code.txt` for code-language
                features; `binding_api.txt` for Layer-1 parity)."""]
        [item """Add the fixture block following existing format."""]
        [item """Run the runner (`devbox run -- make test-vcx` for V
                conformance; `make test-binding-api-parity` for Layer-1
                cross-binding)."""]
        [item """If the runner errors on your fixture, the implementation
                doesn't handle it — that's the bug; file it. If runner
                green, your fixture is now a regression gate."""]]]

    [child id=propose-adr n=10.5.3 title='Proposing a design change'
      [body
        """CX changes that affect the spec / ABI / surface are made by
           editing the spec — the spec is the single source of truth.
           The workflow:"""]
      [list
        [item """**Draft** the change as an edit to the relevant spec
                file under `spec/`, with was-vs-is tables, context,
                the specific decisions, alternatives considered, and
                conformance gates."""]
        [item """**Register** any new backlog item in
                `docs-src/canonical/backlog.cxd` with `:status
                draft`."""]
        [item """**Review window** — submit for owner + community
                review. Iterate the tables until reviewers can scan
                the design in 2-3 minutes."""]
        [item """**Ratify** — flip status to `accepted` in
                `backlog.cxd`."""]
        [item """**Implement** — landing PRs cite the ratified spec
                change. Its conformance gates block the next
                release."""]]
      [body
        """Keep spec edits scannable: lead with was-vs-is tables and
           keep the prose tight so reviewers can grasp the design
           quickly."""]]

    [child id=ship-binding n=10.5.4 title='Shipping a new binding'
      [body
        """Contributing a binding for a language not currently in the
           Tier-1 set (V / Python / Go / Rust):"""]
      [list
        [item """Implement the 16-method Layer-1 surface
                (spec/bindings.md §2.1) — case-adjusted for host
                conventions but otherwise identical."""]
        [item """FFI extern declarations against the C ABI symbols in
                `include/cx.h`. Match the version's cap bits."""]
        [item """Call `cx_init()` once per process; call
                `cx_thread_register()` at every FFI chokepoint (or
                use a per-thread guard pattern)."""]
        [item """Add a quickstart in `docs-src/canonical/sections/07-bindings.cxd`."""]
        [item """Wire conformance — your binding must pass
                `conformance/binding_api.txt` byte-identically (gate
                28.6). The runner pattern lives at
                `lang/python/conformance_code.py` /
                `lang/go/cxlib/conformance_code_test.go` —
                mirror in your language."""]
        [item """PR to `lang/<your-name>/cxlib/` with the binding code
                plus the conformance harness."""]]
      [body
        """For restoring an archived binding (TypeScript / Java / C# /
           Ruby / Kotlin / Swift): see
           `lang/_archived/README.md` for the recipe."""]]

    [child id=debug-investigate n=10.5.5 title='Debugging an implementation'
      [body
        """Reproducing and triaging a CX bug:"""]
      [list
        [item """**Reduce the repro.** Get to the smallest input that
                triggers the failure (one CX file, ideally < 20
                lines)."""]
        [item """**Capture diagnostic output.** `cx eval --trace`
                shows per-directive timing + span emission;
                `cx eval --explain` shows the AST + dispatch path."""]
        [item """**Bisect** if the bug appeared between versions —
                `git bisect run sh -c 'cx eval repro.cx; test $? = 0'`."""]
        [item """**Check the conformance suite** — does a similar
                fixture exist? If yes, what's different about yours?"""]
        [item """**File a fixture** alongside the bug report (see
                §[[add-fixture]]) so the fix lands a regression gate."""]]
      [body
        """For V-side debugging: the impl lives at `vcx/code/*.v`
           (post-rename, was `vcx/programs/`). Build with `devbox run
           -- make -C vcx build`; run unit tests with `make test-vcx`."""]]

    [child id=memory-update n=10.5.6 title='Updating the project memory'
      [body
        """The project memory (`memory/` directory in this repo's
           CLAUDE.md context) tracks long-running state across
           sessions: design decisions, deferred work, known issues,
           perf state. When you land a decision or surface a new
           issue, update the relevant memory file. The convention is
           in CLAUDE.md and the `memory/MEMORY.md` index."""]]]
]
